      "reading": "This is the first test that SEPARATES the two survivors. Raw scatter left them close (3.5% vs 4.39%), but their residuals behave differently: H_coth's residuals are essentially structureless (r = 0.0485 vs A, lag-1 autocorrelation -0.0746), while H_FH_Z's carry a strong systematic trend (r = 0.799, autocorrelation 0.526). A correctly-specified model should leave structureless residuals, so the drift counts AGAINST the Vol^(-1/3) reading and IN FAVOUR of coth-saturation.",
      "caveat": "Not decisive, for one specific reason: the per-pair Coulomb unit is held at its A=3 value throughout, so any true A-dependence of the strong bond B_pp would appear as exactly this kind of drift -- and would land on whichever hypothesis does not happen to absorb it. Bounding B_pp (bean qou-gcmn) is required before this can be called a result rather than evidence."
